```
ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: yellow
REAL_USE_CASE: Teams deploying agentic tool routers with HARD enum-constrained decoding (OpenAI strict mode, Outlines, XGrammar, vLLM guided JSON) where the available tool set is a narrow subset of possible user intents and out-of-set requests occur in production; the decoder must pick a valid tool name and cannot abstain.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Mechanism is real and safety-relevant (monitorability collapse: schema-validate+retry recall = 0 by construction; GAD recovery = 0.0000; escape-hatch leaks at near-miss), but L0 is a geometric similarity-kernel proxy, NOT a real LM (packet HONEST CAVEAT). Kernel-independence proves the (K, neighbor-gap) laws are not a tuned-knob artifact, yet absolute rates and the near-miss confidence effect are not validated on real logits. Microbench-only until L1 confirms on real LMs + real constrained backends.
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [Production pipelines already rely on constrained decoding for reliability; removing it reintroduces malformed-output risk. Escape-hatch ('other'/ASK_USER) is common but recall collapses to 0.000–0.198 at near-miss per R5, so it does not blunt the dangerous case. Fix requires out-of-set detection BEFORE constraining (semantic similarity threshold, intent-space coverage check, or two-stage routing), which adds latency and complexity. Teams may resist because (a) enum cardinality K is often small by design (cost/latency), increasing out-of-set exposure per R1 (0.976 at K=3, 0.650 at K=50), and (b) current monitors only check schema validity, not semantic plausibility.]
RATIONALE: Packet L0 demonstrates kernel-independent monotone laws: misroute rate = P(out-of-set) rising as K falls (0.650→0.976) identical across 6 temp×noise cells (R1); near-miss confidence rises as gap shrinks at every temp (0.05: 0.637→0.801; 0.15: 0.332→0.480; 0.40: 0.182→0.235) (R2); validity-monitor recall = 0.0 (R3); GAD out-of-set gap-recovery = 0.0000 (R4) confirming support-removal is outside GAD's within-support class (Park/Geng 2405.21047, per packet); escape-recall collapses at near-miss (0.000–0.198) while ~1.0 at far gaps (R5). However, HONEST CAVEAT states "L0 is a geometric similarity-kernel proxy, NOT a real LM — it establishes the MECHANISM + the monotone (K x neighbor-gap) laws, not absolute real-model rates." Production relevance requires L1 on real LMs (Llama-3.1-8B/Qwen2.5-7B) with real constrained backends (Outlines/XGrammar/vLLM guided JSON) on BFCL/ToolBench slices, which is not yet provided. Ecological question (c) remains open: do deployments hard-constrain to narrow enum with out-of-set traffic and NO escape hatch by default? Packet notes OpenAI strict/Outlines/XGrammar are dominant but escape-hatch prevalence is unmeasured. Without L1, operational significance is plausible but unproven; the negative result (monitorability collapse) is actionable guidance—do not rely on schema validity alone; add out-of-set detection—but the magnitude of the win in production is insufficient evidence.
```
